# Deliberate exception to the repository-wide `.env.production` rule.
#
# That rule exists for server-side env files, which hold real secrets. This one cannot: Vite
# exposes only VITE_-prefixed variables and compiles them into the JavaScript served to every
# browser, so its contents are public by definition. Tracking it means a production build is
# correct on any machine instead of depending on someone creating the file first — which is
# what stops a deployed site from quietly calling http://localhost:8000.
#
# Do not put anything secret in it. Anything here ships to the browser.
!.env.production
